{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The exported-runner API, fixture counts, numerical tolerances, tie rules, timeouts and single-GPU process lifecycle remain unspecified, so the audit is not yet reproducible.",
    "The live model must demonstrably contain the selected exported checkpoint's weights; comparing the final training state with an earlier selected checkpoint could produce a misleading parity failure.",
    "Fault injection into input fixtures alone cannot exercise internal readout, checkpoint-loading or routing faults. The report needs concrete isolated injection points in the actual exported execution path.",
    "The supplied workflow describes deletion/masking across three draws, while the reported results concern matched substitutions and swaps across ten replicates. Those results cannot characterize the current implementation without version provenance.",
    "Sampled-candidate parity does not cover full-catalog unseen-item filtering and chunked top-k recommendations for the twenty simulator users.",
    "Originality 4/10 is reasonable. Potential 8/10 and difficulty 5/10 remain provisional because runner availability, integration cost and runtime are unmeasured. No supplied evidence establishes that deployment auditing should take priority over completing consumed-event replay."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Resolve the deployment integration and checkpoint-comparison requirements before treating the audit as executable.",
      "query": "For PyTorch recommendation models with separately generated inference scripts, what reproducible differential-testing protocol exercises the actual exported entry point in a fresh process, verifies that the live reference uses the identical selected checkpoint and item mapping, observes preprocessing without replacing it, and runs sequentially on one GPU? Include artifact manifests, subprocess timeouts, serialization precision and dtype-specific score tolerances."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make fault calibration meaningful and cover both benchmark scoring and simulator recommendation behavior.",
      "query": "How should metamorphic and mutation testing validate a BERT4Rec exported predictor using left-padded histories and appended-mask inference? Specify isolated internal mutations for count-minus-one readout, omitted mask, swapped item mapping and wrong category routing; independently verified mutation applicability; deterministic tie handling; and full-catalog unseen-item filtering with chunked top-k parity."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Prevent stale diagnostic evidence and unsupported priority or impact claims from directing the remaining search budget.",
      "query": "What experiment-provenance and budgeted evaluation practices support choosing between deployment-parity auditing and consumed-batch supervision replay in sequential recommendation? Address linking metrics to exact diagnostic code versions and checkpoints, distinguishing three-draw deletion probes from ten-replicate substitution probes, bounding audit runtime, and evaluating downstream value using a fixed validation protocol without adaptive validation overfitting."
    }
  ]
}
